      "message": "perf(sim): sample verifier island planes at cut levels [HELD: equivalence failed]\n\nLaw (c) builds its model planes from the cut levels plus the deepest cut\n(#3615) instead of one plane per feed chord. A ramp emits one feed move\nper thinned vertex, each with its own Z, so the per-chord set made about\n1,700 planes where the path has 3 cut levels.\n\nThis is HELD, not a fix. The all-plane equivalence pin is red: on the\nexisting sloped ramp fixture (ramp_at(500, 36.0)) the surviving planes\nlose 19 part-true ShankHit convictions (moves 274-292) that the\nall-plane reference makes. A less conservative verifier does not merge.\n\nRefs #3615\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Code <noreply@anthropic.com>",
